    "majorFindings": [
      "The codebase shows clear evidence of human authorship - Korean comments in CommandLineBuilder.cs, platform-specific workarounds in NativeMethods.cs, and practical hacks like empty catch blocks for cleanup operations. These idiosyncrasies suggest a developer who has wrestled with real-world Minecraft launcher challenges.",
      "The architecture is well-designed with clear separation between concerns: FileExtractors handle downloads, Installers handle the pipeline, ProcessBuilder handles launch, and Version handling covers all Mojang JSON parsing. This is a mature library.",
      "The version dependency graph handling (in Extensions.cs) shows sophisticated understanding of Minecraft's version inheritance system with circular dependency detection.",
      "The Java version resolution system is particularly impressive, handling multiple platform variants, legacy JRE extraction, and manifest-based discovery.",
      "Several areas need improvement: the ParallelGameInstaller has a clear bug with ThreadLocal not being disposed, multiple empty catch blocks could mask real errors, and there's no retry logic for transient HTTP failures which would significantly impact reliability."
